# Who owns what (requirements-driven collaboration between humans and AI).
#
# The requirements (requirements/, their pictures diagrams/0.* and images/0.*), the front page that says how we work
# (README.md and its picture) and the governance files (.github/, CLAUDE.md) are the human's: every change to them needs @olljanat's approval. Everything else - the design, the
# pictures, the scripts, the layout - is the AI's: every change needs @olljanat-ai's review, which checks that it does
# not conflict with the requirements.
#
# The author of a pull request cannot approve it, and the AI account writes most of them, so branch protection's
# "require review from code owners" cannot enforce this. The required status check `Approvals`
# (.github/workflows/approvals.yml, scripts/approvals.py) does: it reads this file from the pull request's base and
# passes once every owner of a changed file is the author or has approved the latest changes to their files.
# The last matching line wins, as on GitHub.
#
# The lab examples (examples/lab/) are the documentation agent's: generated from Git by onek8s/aks-ai-agents
# (`aks-agent docs lab`, aks-terraform's Lab examples workflow), not the requirements or the design, in neither PDF.
# Their line names no owner, so a pull request that changes only them needs no approval; the human merges it.

*               @olljanat-ai

/requirements/  @olljanat
/diagrams/0.*   @olljanat
/images/0.*     @olljanat
/.github/       @olljanat
/CLAUDE.md      @olljanat
/README.md      @olljanat
/diagrams/how-we-work.mmd  @olljanat
/images/how-we-work.*      @olljanat
/examples/lab/
